Revision history for Perl distribution App-UpdateConfig

1.02 - ????-??-??
 - Use cpanm, when available, to install the missing modules.
 - Install the missing modules globally (with sudo if needed) when the program
   is itself installed globally.
 - Fix the installation command in the README, which did not install the
   optional modules.
 - Accept the MERGE formats in any case (e.g. MERGE TOML).
 - Add a DIR directive to set the directory of the target file.
 - Allow fragments with the same name in different directories, and fail when
   several fragments are applied to the same file with the same guard suffix.
 - Save the state of the MERGE fragments per target file and guard suffix, and
   allow GUARD SUFFIX with MERGE to merge several fragments into the same file.
   The states saved by the previous version are not reused.
 - Use the suffix between brackets in the name of a fragment (e.g. "foo [bar]")
   as its default guard suffix. Fragments that rely on this name without a
   GUARD SUFFIX directive will add a new block in their target file, instead of
   updating the existing one.
 - Use the suffix between brackets in the name of a directory (e.g. "[bar]" or
   "foo [bar]") as the default guard suffix of the fragments that it contains.

1.01 - 2026-10-26
 - Add support for a MERGE directive to handle structured formats.

1.00 - 2026-10-26
 - Initial release to the public repo.
